# {{PROJECT}} glossary (L3)

The ubiquitous language of {{PROJECT}}. **Use these names exactly. Do not introduce synonyms.**

A term is in this glossary when it means something specific to {{PROJECT}} and getting it wrong
produces wrong work. Ordinary English is not defined here.

This file exists because the most expensive misunderstandings in a project are the ones where two
people, or a person and an agent, use the same word for different things and neither notices.

## How to use it

- Code, API fields, database columns, issue titles, contracts and skills **MUST** use the canonical
  term. Where an implementation already uses a different name, that name is recorded in the `Also
  appears as` column and the drift is a work item, not a second definition.
- A new term is added in the same change that introduces it. Coining a term without adding a row is
  how a project ends up with three names for one concept.
- A term that is retired **MUST NOT** be deleted. Mark it `retired` and name the replacement, so a
  reader who finds the old word in old code can resolve it.
- Every definition carries a provenance token. A term with no source is a term someone made up in a
  meeting.

